  partName: Intake Manifold Bolt
  description: The Intake Manifold Bolt is a small, elongated bolt situated at the
    middle-right-front of the engine, responsible for fastening the intake manifold
    to the engine block. This bolt is essential for maintaining a secure connection
    between the intake manifold and the engine, allowing for proper airflow and fuel
    delivery. Notably, the Intake Manifold Bolt's position and material, Material.001,
    are carefully designed to minimize stress and vibration.
